      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hot-press sintering of the coating promotes Hf-Zr interdiffusion and formation of a transition layer.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::008::3_results_and_discussion",
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Exposure at temperatures up to approximately 1600 °C for a short duration is representative of LOCA steam-oxidation conditions for pressurized-water-reactor cladding.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "During high-temperature steam exposure, the hafnium coating will oxidize into a continuous, dense HfO2 layer.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "An Hf-Zr interdiffusion zone will enhance adhesion between the coating and zirconium-alloy cladding.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hafnium has a strong affinity for oxygen.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hafnium preferentially forms HfO2 when exposed to high-temperature steam.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC10488483::web::016::4_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting HfO2 is chemically stable and compact.",
